#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:3
msgid "Highlights"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:5
msgid "Shape-typing support for almost all of the NumPy API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:7
#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:846
msgid "(`gh-32835 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32835>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:11
msgid "New functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:14
msgid "New function `numpy.top_k`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:16
msgid ""
"A new function ``np.top_k(array, k, axis=..., mode=..., sorted=...)`` was "
"added, which returns the largest/smallest k values of an array along a given "
"axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:20
msgid "(`gh-31659 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31659>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:23
msgid "New function `numpy.minmax`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:25
msgid ""
"A new function ``np.minmax(a, axis=..., out=..., keepdims=..., initial=..., "
"where=...)`` was added, which returns a ``(min, max)`` tuple holding the "
"minimum and the maximum of an array along a given axis.  It is equivalent to "
"``(np.min(a, ...), np.max(a, ...))`` but computes both in a single fused "
"pass over the data.  For dtypes that support ``min``/``max`` but have no "
"fused ``minmax`` loop (such as the string DType and other user DTypes), it "
"falls back to two separate reductions.  A masked-array counterpart ``np.ma."
"minmax`` was also added, which simply returns ``(np.ma.min(a, ...), np.ma."
"max(a, ...))``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:34
msgid "(`gh-32231 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32231>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:38
msgid "Deprecations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:41
msgid "``numpy.linalg.lapack_lite`` is deprecated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:43
msgid ""
"Importing ``numpy.linalg.lapack_lite`` is deprecated. The module is an "
"internal implementation detail of `numpy.linalg` and was never intended as a "
"public API. Users that need LAPACK or BLAS routines should use ``scipy."
"linalg.lapack`` or ``scipy.linalg.blas`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:48
msgid "(`gh-32015 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32015>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:52
msgid "Expired deprecations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:54
msgid ""
"The deprecated ``'full'``, ``'f'``, ``'economic'``, and ``'e'`` modes of "
"`numpy.linalg.qr` have been removed. These were deprecated in NumPy 1.8. Use "
"``'reduced'`` instead of ``'full'``/``'f'``, and ``'raw'`` instead of "
"``'economic'``/``'e'``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:59
msgid "(`gh-31387 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31387>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:61
msgid ""
"The ``numpy.typing.mypy_plugin`` mypy plugin (deprecated since NumPy 2.3) "
"did not affect type-safety and has been removed in favor of platform- and "
"type-checker-agnostic static typing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:65
msgid "(`gh-31931 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31931>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:69
msgid "Compatibility notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:72
msgid "`numpy.insert` out-of-bounds index detection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:73
msgid ""
"``numpy.insert`` now consistently raises ``IndexError`` for any out-of-"
"bounds index, including when out-of-bounds and in-bounds indices are mixed "
"in the same call. Previously such cases could silently succeed or produce "
"incorrect results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:78
msgid "(`gh-31782 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31782>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:81
msgid "``ufunc.reduce`` on a multi-output ufunc now raises ``TypeError``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:82
msgid ""
"Calling :meth:`~numpy.ufunc.reduce` on a ufunc with more than one output "
"that does not register a reduction loop now raises a :exc:`TypeError` "
"instead of a :exc:`ValueError`. Of NumPy's own ufuncs only `numpy.divmod` is "
"affected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:87
#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:168
msgid "(`gh-31816 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31816>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:90
msgid ""
"Casting and validation changes for fixed-width to variable-width string "
"conversions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:91
msgid ""
"Casts from fixed-width `numpy.bytes_` and `numpy.str_` arrays to `numpy."
"dtypes.StringDType` are now considered `\"safe\"` rather than `\"same-"
"kind\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:94
msgid ""
"These casts from `numpy.bytes_` to `numpy.dtypes.StringDType` now validate "
"the bytes are valid UTF-8 and raise a ``UnicodeDecodeError`` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:96
msgid ""
"Casting a fixed-width `numpy.void_` array containing invalid UTF-8 now "
"triggers a ``UnicodeDecodeError`` rather than a ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:99
#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:415
msgid "(`gh-32095 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32095>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:102
msgid "Python scalar promotion and casting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:104
msgid ""
"`numpy.concatenate` with ``axis=None`` and `numpy.choose` now raise "
"``OverflowError`` for Python integers outside the result dtype's range, "
"instead of wrapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:107
msgid ""
"Ufuncs, `numpy.copyto`, and `numpy.concatenate` now enforce the same Python "
"scalar restrictions for ``casting=\"no\"`` as for ``casting=\"equiv\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:110
msgid ""
"See :ref:`arrays.promotion.python-scalar-casting` for the detailed rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:112
#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:258
msgid "(`gh-32497 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32497>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:115
msgid "StringDType NaN-like inequality comparisons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:116
msgid ""
"Inequality comparisons involving a NaN-like ``StringDType`` missing value "
"now return ``True``, matching floating-point NaN behavior. Previously, both "
"equality and inequality returned ``False``. Equality and ordered comparisons "
"still return ``False`` for NaN-like missing values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:121
msgid ""
"Filtering with ``arr[arr != \"excluded\"]`` therefore retains NaN-like "
"missing values. To exclude them, use ``arr[(~np.isnan(arr)) & (arr != "
"\"excluded\")]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:124
#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:462
msgid "(`gh-32564 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32564>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:128
msgid "C API changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:131
msgid "NumPy DTypes are heap-allocated and can use ``PyType_FromMetaType``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:132
msgid ""
"Most of NumPy DType classes, except ``np.dtype`` itself, are now heap-"
"allocated types and downstream DTypes can now create their own DType classes "
"using ``PyType_FromMetaType``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:136
msgid ""
"DType authors using ``PyArrayInitDTypeMeta_FromSpec`` may notice this if the "
"DType has incorrect reference counting, since DTypes are no longer immortal. "
"In theory this also means that you cannot subclass abstract DTypes anymore "
"unless converting your DType to a heap-allocated type itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:141
msgid "(`gh-31364 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31364>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:144
msgid "``PyArray_StringDTypeObject`` is opaque under the abi3t stable ABI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:146
msgid ""
"The ``PyArray_StringDTypeObject`` was accidentally exposed in NumPy 2.5 when "
"targeting the free-threading-compatible stable ABI (``Py_TARGET_ABI3T``). "
"``PyArray_StringDTypeObject`` is now an opaque struct: extensions compiled "
"that way cannot access its fields, since the struct layout depends on the "
"size of the object header. Any code that accessed "
"``PyArray_StringDTypeObject`` fields in an abi3t build would have crashed, "
"so we are making this API change in a bugfix release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:155
msgid ""
"The ``NpyString`` allocator API remains usable by passing the descriptor "
"object pointer, e.g. "
"``NpyString_acquire_allocator((PyArray_StringDTypeObject *)descr)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:159
msgid "(`gh-31771 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31771>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:162
msgid ""
"New mechanism to register reduction loops to ufuncs for multi-output "
"reductions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:163
msgid ""
"Ufuncs with more than one output can now support :meth:`~numpy.ufunc.reduce` "
"by registering a dedicated reduction loop (and, optionally, per-output "
"identities) on their ``ArrayMethod``. The reduction returns one array per "
"output. See :ref:`c-api.reduction-loop-tutorial` for a worked example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:171
msgid "``PyArray`` allocator helpers are now deprecated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:173
msgid ""
"The following macro and C API helper functions for allocating data are now "
"`soft-deprecated <https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-soft-"
"deprecated>`_:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:177
msgid "``NPY_USE_PYMEM``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:178
msgid "``PyArray_malloc``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:179
msgid "``PyArray_realloc``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:180
msgid "``PyArray_free``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:182
msgid ""
"If you are using these in your extensions, we suggest migrating to use `the "
"Python Raw Memory Interface instead <https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/memory."
"html#raw-memory-interface>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:186
msgid "(`gh-32334 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32334>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:190
msgid "New Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:193
msgid "Recognize ISO Fortran Environment kinds in F2Py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:195
msgid ""
"This adds the ``int16``, ``int32``, and ``int64`` integer kinds and the "
"``real32`` and ``real64`` real kinds from the ISO Fortran Environment module "
"to F2Py."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:199
msgid "(`gh-28574 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/28574>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:202
msgid ""
"New ``descending`` keyword argument for `numpy.partition` and `numpy."
"argpartition`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:203
msgid ""
"Users can now pass the ``descending=True`` keyword argument to `numpy."
"partition` and `numpy.argpartition` to partition and argpartition arrays in "
"descending order. NaN values, if present, are partitioned to the end of the "
"array in both ascending and descending sorts. This feature is available for "
"all built-in dtypes except ``void`` and ``generic``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:209
msgid "(`gh-31511 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31511>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:212
msgid "DType partitioning and argpartitioning supports the ArrayMethod API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:213
msgid ""
"User-defined dtypes can now implement custom partitioning and "
"argpartitioning using the ArrayMethod API in a fashion similar to sorting "
"and argsorting. These methods are used by `numpy.partition` and `numpy."
"argpartition` when called with arrays of the user-defined dtype."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:218
msgid ""
"The partitioning and argpartitioning methods are registered by passing the "
"arraymethod specs that implement the operations to the "
"`PyUFunc_AddLoopsFromSpecs` function. See the ``ArrayMethod`` API "
"documentation for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:222
msgid "(`gh-31614 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31614>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:225
msgid "Add DLPack support to NumPy scalars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:226
msgid ""
"``scalar.__dlpack__`` and ``scalar.__dlpack_device__`` methods have been "
"added to NumPy scalars to allow exporting them to DLPack, similarly to "
"ndarrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:229
msgid "(`gh-32029 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32029>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:232
msgid "``numpy.ma.unwrap`` has been added"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:233
msgid ""
"`numpy.ma.unwrap` is the mask-aware equivalent of `numpy.unwrap`. It skips "
"over the masked elements, computing each correction from the delta to the "
"closest preceding unmasked element rather than from the data underlying the "
"mask, and carries the mask through to the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:238
msgid "(`gh-32091 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32091>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:241
msgid ""
"Size inference when converting ``StringDType`` arrays to fixed-width strings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:242
msgid ""
"Previously, converting a `numpy.dtypes.StringDType` array to a fixed-width "
"string dtype with an unspecified size, such as ``arr.astype(np.str_)`` or "
"``np.array(arr, dtype=\"S\")``, raised a ``TypeError`` asking for an "
"explicit size. NumPy now inspects the array values and infers a size big "
"enough to store the widest entry without truncation, matching the existing "
"behavior when converting sequences of Python strings. Passing an explicit "
"size still truncates entries that do not fit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:250
msgid "(`gh-32097 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32097>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:254
msgid "Improvements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:260
msgid "StringDType comparisons now correctly handle embedded NULL bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:262
msgid "(`gh-31662 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31662>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:264
msgid ""
"`numpy.i0` no longer returns ``inf`` for large inputs such as ``np."
"i0(713.0)``. The function now avoids intermediate overflow and returns the "
"correct finite value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:266
msgid ""
"`numpy.i0(np.inf)` no longer triggers a spurious ``RuntimeWarning`` due to "
"divide-by-zero in the implementation and returns `np.inf` rather than `np."
"nan`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:268
msgid "(`gh-32223 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32223>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:270
msgid ""
"`np.copyto`, `np.full`, `np.where`, `np.concatenate` with ``axis=None``, and "
"`np.choose` now convert an exact Python ``str`` scalar directly with the "
"resolved dtype instead of through a fixed-width unicode intermediate, so a "
"trailing null is no longer lost for ``StringDType`` or ``object``. For "
"example, ``np.full(2, \"x\\0\", dtype=np.dtypes.StringDType())[0]`` now "
"gives ``\"x\\0\"`` rather than ``\"x\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:277
msgid "(`gh-32356 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32356>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:279
msgid ""
"Casting a StringDType array to bool now correctly handles missing data that "
"is a string. Previously it would treat an empty string as truthy and a non-"
"empty string as falsey."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:282
msgid "`numpy.nonzero` now correctly classifies non-empty strings as nonzero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:284
msgid "(`gh-32418 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32418>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:286
msgid ""
"`numpy.minimum` and `numpy.maximum` along with the ``min`` and ``max`` "
"reductions now correctly handle cases when one operand is a fixed-width "
"string array and one operand is StringDType. These cases used to raise "
"`numpy._UFuncNoLoopError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:291
msgid "(`gh-32419 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32419>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:293
msgid "Added support for dividing ``timedelta64`` by ``bool``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:295
msgid "(`gh-32555 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32555>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:297
msgid ""
"`numpy.linalg.svd` and `numpy.linalg.lstsq` now raise for inputs containing "
"infinities instead of returning garbage results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:298
msgid ""
"Fixed hangs in `numpy.linalg.svd` and `numpy.linalg.lstsq` for certain "
"inputs containing infinities for recent versions of some LAPACK "
"implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:299
msgid "`numpy.linalg.cond` now handles non-finite inputs more consistently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:301
msgid "(`gh-32593 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32593>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:304
msgid "`np.show_runtime` has display modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:306
msgid ""
"``np.show_runtime`` now has a new optional parameter ``mode`` to help "
"customize the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:309
msgid "(`gh-26255 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/26255>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:312
msgid "`numpy.common_type` now raises a clear error for non-array input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:313
msgid ""
"Passing a dtype or scalar type to `numpy.common_type`, such as ``np."
"common_type(np.dtype(\"f4\"))``, used to raise a confusing "
"``AttributeError``. It now raises a ``TypeError`` that points to `numpy."
"result_type` and `numpy.promote_types`, which are the tools meant for "
"combining dtypes and scalar types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:319
msgid "(`gh-30890 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/30890>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:322
msgid ""
"``nanmean``, ``nanstd`` and ``nanvar`` no longer fail on read-only reductions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:323
msgid ""
"These functions divide the running sum by the count in place, which assumed "
"the sum was writeable. When it was not they raised ``ValueError: output "
"array is read-only`` instead of returning a result and they now allocate the "
"output in that case, keeping the dtype the in-place divide would have "
"produced. This is what made ``np.nanmean``, ``np.nanstd`` and ``np.nanvar`` "
"fail on a ``MaskedArray`` whose values are all masked, since ``numpy.ma`` "
"reduces that to the read-only ``np.ma.masked``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:331
msgid "(`gh-31069 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31069>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:334
msgid "Structured dtypes now support larger field sizes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:335
msgid ""
"It is now possible to construct structured data types with field sizes and "
"offsets that exceed the size of a standard C integer. Arrays using these "
"structured data types are now also possible to construct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:340
msgid "(`gh-31332 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31332>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:343
msgid "Object and ``StringDType`` array sorting supports ``descending=True``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:344
msgid ""
"`np.sort` and `np.argsort` with arrays of dtype ``object`` or "
"``StringDType`` now support passing `descending=True` to sort in descending "
"order. Objects that compare as not equal to themselves (``obj != obj``), "
"such as NaN-like objects, and missing strings with a nan-like ``na_object`` "
"are considered unordered and are sorted to the end of the array, regardless "
"of the value of ``descending``. Because `np.partition` and `np.argpartition` "
"fall back to a full sort for these dtypes, they now accept "
"``descending=True`` for them as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:352
msgid ""
"(`gh-31431 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31431>`__, `gh-32286 "
"<https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32286>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:355
msgid "``np.linspace`` no longer returns NaN for equal infinite endpoints"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:356
msgid ""
"``np.linspace(np.inf, np.inf, N)`` (and ``-np.inf``) now correctly returns "
"an array filled with ``inf`` instead of ``nan``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:359
msgid "(`gh-31620 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31620>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:362
msgid ""
"``numpy.unwrap`` is now implemented as a generalized ufunc and preserves "
"array subclasses"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:363
msgid ""
"The core of ``numpy.unwrap`` is now a generalized ufunc in C++ (signature "
"``(n),(),()->(n)``) covering the floating point and signed integer dtypes "
"while performing the operation in a single pass without the intermediate "
"arrays the previous Python implementation had to allocate. As a result, "
"``numpy.unwrap`` now preserves the ``ndarray`` subclasses rather than always "
"returning a base ``ndarray``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:369
msgid "(`gh-31848 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31848>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:372
msgid "``DataSource`` accepts path-like local paths"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:373
msgid ""
"``numpy.lib._datasource.DataSource`` and ``Repository`` now accept ``os."
"PathLike`` local paths in the same places that accepted string paths. This "
"includes ``open``, ``exists``, and ``abspath`` methods, as well as the "
"module-level ``numpy.lib._datasource.open`` helper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:378
msgid "(`gh-31906 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31906>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:381
msgid "``f2py`` handles platform-specific separators in ``--include-paths``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:382
msgid ""
"``f2py --include-paths`` now splits include directories using the platform "
"path separator, fixing parsing of Windows paths containing drive letters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:385
msgid "(`gh-31934 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31934>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:388
msgid "StringDType ``partition`` accepts ``str`` separators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:389
msgid ""
"`np.strings.partition` and `np.strings.rpartition` now accept a Python "
"``str`` or fixed-width unicode separator when operating on ``StringDType`` "
"arrays. Previously the separator had to be a ``StringDType`` array itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:393
#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:964
msgid "(`gh-32040 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32040>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:396
msgid "Ensure F2Py defines required typedefs in generated C wrapper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:398
msgid ""
"Ensure F2Py includes the typedefs required for kinds in the ISO C Binding "
"module and the ISO Fortran Environment module in the generated C wrapper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:402
msgid ""
"This also allows the ``int8`` integer kind from the ISO Fortran Environment "
"module and the ``c_int8_t`` integer kind from the ISO C Binding module to "
"work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:406
msgid "(`gh-32043 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32043>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:409
msgid "Fixed-width string to ``StringDType`` casts are now safe and validated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:410
msgid ""
"The casts from fixed-width `numpy.bytes_` and `numpy.str_` to `numpy.dtypes."
"StringDType` are now marked `\"safe\"` rather than `\"same-kind\"`. We also "
"now validate that `numpy.bytes_`, `numpy.void`, and `numpy.str_` arrays "
"contain valid UTF-8 before converting to `numpy.dtypes.StringDType`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:418
msgid ""
"np.positive no longer raises _UfuncNoLoopError when called on boolean arrays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:419
msgid ""
"``np.positive`` and the unary ``+`` operator now register a loop for boolean "
"arrays. ``np.positive(np.array([True, False]))`` now returns ``[True, "
"False]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:422
msgid "(`gh-32100 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32100>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:425
msgid "Improved error for non-ASCII ``nditer`` flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:426
msgid ""
"``numpy.nditer`` and ``numpy.nested_iters`` now read flag names from Python "
"strings instead of encoding them to ASCII first. Flags containing non-ASCII "
"characters used to raise ``UnicodeEncodeError``, but now raise "
"``ValueError``, which makes it consistent with the error given for other "
"unrecognized flag names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:428
msgid "(`gh-32232 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32232>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:431
msgid "`numpy.digitize` preserves integer ordering for large values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:433
msgid ""
"`numpy.digitize` no longer loses ordering information for large integer bin "
"edges that cannot be distinguished after conversion to ``float64``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:436
msgid "(`gh-32467 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32467>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:439
msgid "StringDType hashing with NaN sentinels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:440
msgid ""
"``StringDType`` instances with equivalent floating-point NaN sentinels now "
"have equal hashes. Previously, distinct NaN objects could produce equal "
"dtype instances with different hashes, causing dictionary lookups and set "
"deduplication to fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:445
msgid "(`gh-32563 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32563>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:448
msgid "StringDType missing-value handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:449
msgid ""
"NumPy's array equality assertions now handle matching missing values in "
"``StringDType`` arrays whose sentinel is a NumPy floating-point NaN, such as "
"``numpy.float32(\"nan\")``. Previously, these assertions could incorrectly "
"report unequal arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:454
msgid ""
"For `numpy.unique`, requesting indices, inverse indices, or counts now "
"handles NaN-like sentinels consistently: ``equal_nan=True`` groups missing "
"entries, while ``equal_nan=False`` keeps them separate. With "
"``return_index=True``, the index returned for grouped missing values now "
"identifies their first occurrence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:459
msgid ""
"Comparisons also correctly distinguish ``None``-like missing values from "
"empty strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:465
msgid "``np.repeat`` accepts any integer dtype as ``repeats``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:466
msgid ""
"`numpy.repeat` now casts ``repeats`` with same-kind casting, like `numpy."
"take`. Integer arrays such as ``uint64``, or ``int64`` on 32-bit platforms, "
"no longer raise a ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:469
msgid "(`gh-32665 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32665>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:472
msgid "``np.put`` accepts any integer dtype as indices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:473
msgid ""
"`numpy.put` now casts ``ind`` with same-kind casting, like `numpy.take`. "
"Integer arrays such as ``uint64``, or ``int64`` on 32-bit platforms, no "
"longer raise a ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:476
msgid "(`gh-32666 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32666>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:479
msgid "``np.choose`` accepts any integer dtype as indices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:480
msgid ""
"`numpy.choose` now casts ``a`` with same-kind casting, like `numpy.take`. "
"Integer arrays such as ``uint64``, or ``int64`` on 32-bit platforms, no "
"longer raise a ``TypeError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:483
msgid "(`gh-32667 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32667>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:486
msgid "``np.searchsorted`` accepts any integer dtype as ``sorter``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:487
msgid ""
"`numpy.searchsorted` now casts ``sorter`` with same-kind casting, like "
"`numpy.take`. Integer arrays such as ``uint64``, or ``int64`` on 32-bit "
"platforms, no longer raise an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:490
msgid "(`gh-32668 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32668>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:493
msgid "``open_memmap`` accepts integer-like objects in ``shape``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:494
msgid ""
"`numpy.lib.format.open_memmap` now accepts integer-like objects in ``shape`` "
"similar to `numpy.memmap`. Before, non Python ints would lead to a corrupt "
"header in the `.npy` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:498
msgid "(`gh-32698 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32698>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:501
msgid "``np.log`` no longer warns when propagating complex NaNs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:502
msgid ""
"For complex inputs with at least one NaN component and no infinite "
"component, `numpy.log` now returns ``NaN + NaN j`` without emitting an "
"invalid floating-point warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:506
msgid "(`gh-32706 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32706>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:509
msgid "``logaddexp`` and ``logaddexp2`` no longer warn for NaN inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:510
msgid ""
"`numpy.logaddexp` and `numpy.logaddexp2` now propagate NaN inputs without "
"emitting an invalid floating-point warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:513
msgid "(`gh-32733 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32733>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:516
msgid "``numpy.reciprocal`` of complex zero now matches division"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:517
msgid ""
"`numpy.reciprocal` of a complex zero now returns ``inf+nanj`` and sets the "
"divide-by-zero floating point flag, matching ``1 / x``. It previously "
"returned ``nan+nanj``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:521
msgid "(`gh-32812 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32812>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:525
msgid "Performance improvements and changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:527
msgid "`numpy.isin` is now much faster for large ``StringDType`` arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:529
msgid "(`gh-32693 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32693>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:532
msgid "Faster ufunc calls through inner-loop caching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:533
msgid ""
"Ufuncs implemented through the legacy ufunc API (which includes most ufuncs "
"provided by NumPy itself) now cache the selected inner-loop function instead "
"of looking it up on every call. This speeds up ufunc calls, most notably for "
"scalar and small-array inputs (roughly 10% faster). Note that as a "
"consequence, loops must be registered through the official API (e.g. "
"``PyUFunc_ReplaceLoopBySignature``); directly modifying the ``functions`` "
"member of a ufunc no longer takes effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:541
msgid "(`gh-31068 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31068>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:544
msgid "Faster selected ``numpy.pad`` modes for zero-width axes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:545
msgid ""
"``numpy.pad`` is now faster for axes with pad width ``(0, 0)`` when using "
"``mode=\"linear_ramp\"`` or one of the statistic modes ``\"maximum\"``, "
"``\"mean\"``, ``\"median\"``, and ``\"minimum\"``. These modes now skip "
"unnecessary mode-specific work for axes where no values are added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:550
msgid "(`gh-31791 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31791>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:553
msgid "Faster reductions on small arrays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:554
msgid ""
"``numpy.sum``, ``numpy.prod``, ``numpy.min``, ``numpy.max``, ``numpy.any``, "
"and ``numpy.all`` are now faster for small arrays. This reduces the Python-"
"level overhead of calling these reductions, which is most noticeable when "
"the reduction itself is cheap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:559
msgid "(`gh-31845 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31845>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:562
msgid "Faster reductions for exact ndarrays"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:563
msgid ""
"`numpy.sum`, `numpy.prod`, `numpy.min`, `numpy.max`, `numpy.amin`, `numpy."
"amax`, `numpy.any`, and `numpy.all` now avoid Python dispatch overhead for "
"exact `numpy.ndarray` inputs, reducing call times for benchmarked small-"
"array reductions by approximately 30%-50%. Subclasses and custom array types "
"continue to use the original ``__array_function__`` dispatch path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:569
msgid "(`gh-32041 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32041>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:572
msgid ""
"Faster method dispatch for ``np.take``, ``np.argsort`` and similar functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:573
msgid ""
"The internal helpers that forward functions such as `numpy.take`, `numpy."
"reshape`, `numpy.transpose`, `numpy.argsort`, `numpy.argmax`, `numpy."
"cumsum`, `numpy.round` and `numpy.searchsorted` to the corresponding ndarray "
"method are now implemented in C. This reduces the Python-level call overhead "
"of about 25 dispatched functions, which is most noticeable for small arrays "
"(typically 5%-30% faster)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:580
msgid "(`gh-32165 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32165>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:583
msgid ""
"Better multithreaded scaling when using float constants on free-threaded "
"Python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:584
msgid ""
"On free-threaded builds, float constants such as ``np.pi`` and ``np.nan`` "
"are now immortal, which removes reference count contention between threads "
"using them concurrently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:588
msgid "(`gh-32513 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32513>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:591
msgid "Faster casts from fixed-width strings and faster ``str_`` scalars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:592
msgid ""
"Casting fixed-width string arrays (``S`` and ``U`` dtypes) to numeric "
"dtypes, for example ``np.array([\"1\", \"2\"]).astype(int)``, is now 1.4-3x "
"faster. Creating `numpy.str_` scalars, for instance when indexing or "
"iterating over a ``U`` array, is about 1.5x faster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:597
msgid "(`gh-32550 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32550>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:600
msgid "Faster standard normal sampling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:601
msgid ""
"`numpy.random.Generator.standard_normal` now applies the sign of each "
"variate with a multiplication rather than a branch on a random bit, which "
"the processor cannot predict. This reduces the time per variate by roughly "
"30% to 40% on x86-64, for both ``float64`` and ``float32``. aarch64 is "
"unaffected, as compilers already emit a conditional select there, and the "
"legacy `numpy.random.RandomState` normal variates are unaffected as they use "
"a different algorithm. The generated stream is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:609
msgid "(`gh-32568 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32568>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:612
msgid "Faster broadcasting in ufuncs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:613
msgid ""
"Ufunc calls such as ``a + v`` with ``a.shape == (n, 3)`` and ``v.shape == "
"(3,)`` that include broadcasts now re-use iterator buffer more reliably. "
"This can lead to significant speed-ups for such operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:617
#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:901
msgid "(`gh-32595 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32595>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:620
msgid "Faster Laplace sampling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:621
msgid ""
"`numpy.random.Generator.laplace` and `numpy.random.RandomState.laplace` now "
"select between the two halves of the inverse CDF without branching on an "
"unpredictable bit, and evaluate a single logarithm rather than one per "
"branch. This reduces the time per variate by roughly 20% on x86-64 and 40% "
"on aarch64. The generated stream is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:627
msgid "(`gh-32601 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32601>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:630
msgid "Descending sorts and partitions are now SIMD accelerated on x86"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:631
msgid ""
"`numpy.sort`, `numpy.argsort`, `numpy.partition` and `numpy.argpartition` "
"with ``descending=True`` no longer fall back to scalar code on x86, and now "
"use the same SIMD kernels as the ascending versions for most integer and "
"floating point dtypes.  On AVX2 this is 2-9x faster than before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:636
msgid "(`gh-32690 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32690>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:640
msgid "Typing improvements and changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:643
msgid "Generic `numpy.object_` type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:644
msgid ""
"The `numpy.object_` scalar type is now a generic type, with its type "
"parameter representing the wrapped Python object, defaulting to ``Any`` if "
"omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:647
msgid "(`gh-32075 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32075>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:650
msgid "Promotion-aware ufunc return types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:651
msgid ""
"All ufuncs in the main namespace are now individually annotated, instead of "
"sharing one generic ``numpy.ufunc`` type. Their ``__call__``, ``reduce``, "
"``accumulate``, ``reduceat``, ``outer``, and ``at`` methods now follow "
"NumPy's promotion rules, so that the output dtype is inferred instead of "
"``Any``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:656
msgid ""
"import numpy as np\n"
"import numpy.typing as npt\n"
"\n"
"x: npt.NDArray[np.float32]\n"
"y: npt.NDArray[np.int16]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(np.sqrt(y))\n"
"# before: npt.NDArray[Any]\n"
"# after:  npt.NDArray[np.float32]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(np.multiply(x, y))\n"
"# before: npt.NDArray[Any]\n"
"# after:  npt.NDArray[np.float32]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:672
msgid ""
"This took 44 pull requests and over 20,000 lines of *hand-written* code, "
"spread over 1,905 overloads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:675
msgid "(`gh-32198 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32198>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:678
msgid "`numpy.random.Generator` shape-typing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:679
msgid ""
"The random sampling methods of `numpy.random.Generator` now use the ``size`` "
"parameter to infer the shape-type of the returned array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:682
msgid ""
"rng = np.random.default_rng()\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(rng.normal(size=(2, 3)))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[float64]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(rng.dirichlet([0.3, 0.7], size=(2, 3)))  # appends a dimension\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[float64]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int, int], dtype[float64]]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:694
msgid "(`gh-32357 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32357>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:697
msgid "`numpy.linalg` shape-typing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:698
msgid ""
"The `numpy.linalg` functions now use the shape-types of their input(s) to "
"infer the shape-type of the returned array(s). Due to limitations of "
"Python's type system, this usually only applies to low-rank array-likes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:702
msgid ""
"A = np.array([[1.1, 1.2], [2.1, 2.2]])\n"
"b = np.array([1.0, 2.0])\n"
"reveal_type(np.linalg.solve(A, b))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[float64]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"stacked = np.array([[[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]]])\n"
"reveal_type(np.linalg.inv(stacked))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[Any]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int, int], dtype[float64]]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:715
msgid "(`gh-32424 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32424>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:718
msgid "`numpy.ndarray` shape-typing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:719
msgid ""
"The methods and operators of `numpy.ndarray` now use the shape-type of the "
"array to infer the shape-type of the result. This includes indexing, "
"iteration, reductions along an ``axis``, and the arithmetic, bitwise, and "
"comparison operators. Due to limitations of Python's type system, binary "
"operators usually only do so for scalar operands and for arrays with the "
"same shape-type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:725
msgid ""
"x = np.ones((2, 3))\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(x[0])\n"
"# before: Any\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(x.sum(axis=0))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[float64]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(x + x)\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[float64]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int], dtype[float64]]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:741
msgid "(`gh-32540 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32540>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:744
msgid "`numpy.lib.stride_tricks` shape-typing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:745
msgid ""
"The `numpy.lib.stride_tricks` functions now use the ``shape`` and "
"``window_shape`` argument types to infer the shape-type of the returned "
"array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:748
msgid ""
"x = np.arange(6.0)\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(np.lib.stride_tricks.as_strided(x, shape=(2, 3)))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[float64]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(np.lib.stride_tricks.sliding_window_view(x, 3))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[float64]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int], dtype[float64]]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:760
msgid "(`gh-32736 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32736>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:763
msgid "``numpy.emath`` shape-typing and dtype inference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:764
msgid ""
"The ``numpy.emath`` functions now infer the shape-type of the returned array "
"from their inputs. For nested sequences this is limited to 1-d and 2-d "
"inputs, and for ``ndarray`` all shape-types are preserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:768
msgid ""
"reveal_type(np.emath.sqrt([-1, 4]))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[Any]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int], dtype[complex128 | float64]]\n"
"\n"
"z = np.array([[1.0, -1.0]], dtype=np.complex64)\n"
"reveal_type(np.emath.log(z))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[complexfloating]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int], dtype[complex64]]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:779
msgid ""
"Scalar return types are also more precise. For floating-point inputs, the "
"return type is a union of the corresponding real and complex scalar types, "
"since the result depends on the input *values*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:783
msgid ""
"reveal_type(np.emath.sqrt(-1.0))\n"
"# before: Any\n"
"# after:  complex128 | float64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:789
msgid "(`gh-32762 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32762>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:792
msgid "`numpy.polynomial` shape-typing and dtype inference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:793
msgid ""
"The `numpy.polynomial` series classes and functions now use the shape-types "
"of their input(s) to infer the shape-type of the returned array. Due to "
"limitations of Python's type system, this usually only applies to low-rank "
"array-likes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:797
msgid ""
"The functions' dtypes and scalar return types are also more precise, e.g. "
"``float64`` instead of ``floating``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:800
msgid "(`gh-32829 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32829>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:803
msgid "Shape-typing for the main ``numpy`` namespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:804
msgid ""
"The functions in the main ``numpy`` namespace now use the shape-types of "
"their input(s) to infer the shape-type of the returned array(s). Due to "
"limitations of Python's type system, this usually only applies to low-rank "
"array-likes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:808
msgid ""
"a = np.array([[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]])\n"
"x = np.array([1.0, 2.0])\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(a)\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[Any]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(np.stack([x, x]))\n"
"# before: ndarray[tuple[Any, ...], dtype[Any]]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(np.sum(a, axis=0))\n"
"# before: ndarray[Any, Any]\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(np.dot(a, x))\n"
"# before: Any\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int], dtype[float64]]\n"
"\n"
"reveal_type(np.percentile(a, [25, 75], axis=0))\n"
"# before: Any\n"
"# after:  ndarray[tuple[int, int], dtype[float64]]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:833
msgid ""
"This allows type-checkers to catch shape mismatches that previously went "
"unnoticed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:835
msgid ""
"def center(v: np.ndarray[tuple[int], np.dtype[np.float64]]) -> None: ...\n"
"\n"
"mu = np.mean(a, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n"
"center(mu)\n"
"# before: no error\n"
"# after:  error: incompatible type \"ndarray[tuple[int, int], "
"dtype[float64]]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:844
msgid "This took 93 pull requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:849
msgid "New ``numpy.typing.Array{0,1,2,3,4}D`` shape-typed array aliases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:850
msgid ""
"``numpy.typing`` now provides the ``Array0D``, ``Array1D``, ``Array2D``, "
"``Array3D``, and ``Array4D`` generic type aliases for arrays with a known "
"number of dimensions. For example, ``npt.Array2D[np.float64]`` is equivalent "
"to ``np.ndarray[tuple[int, int], np.dtype[np.float64]]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:854
msgid "(`gh-32837 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32837>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:857
msgid "Generic ``numpy.poly1d`` and improved type inference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:858
msgid ""
"``numpy.poly1d`` is now generic over the scalar type of its coefficients, to "
"allow for more precise type inference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:861
msgid "(`gh-32850 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32850>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:865
msgid "Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:867
msgid ""
"With a NaN-like ``na_object`` such as ``np.nan``, casting to ``StringDType`` "
"and item assignment now store the missing value for a NaN of any real or "
"complex floating point type.  Missing entries now cast to floating point and "
"complex dtypes as NaN instead of raising an error, so NaN values round-trip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:872
msgid "(`gh-31825 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31825>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:874
msgid "The minimum supported GCC version has been updated from 9.3.0 to 10.3.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:876
msgid "(`gh-31843 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31843>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:878
msgid ""
"Structured dtypes and subarray dtypes containing ``StringDType`` now "
"consistently raise ``TypeError``. Formerly some structured dtpes containing "
"``StringDType`` could be created, but this could lead to data corruption or "
"crashes on array data accesses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:883
msgid "(`gh-32027 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32027>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:885
msgid ""
"``ndarray.byteswap`` now supports dtypes that have no defined byte order (e."
"g. when ``dtype.byteorder == \"|\"``). Such values are left unchanged, "
"including when they occur in structured dtypes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:889
msgid "(`gh-32150 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32150>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:891
msgid ""
"Casting a fixed-width byte string array (``np.bytes_``) to ``StringDType`` "
"now raises ``UnicodeDecodeError`` when the bytes are not valid UTF-8. "
"Previously the invalid bytes were stored as-is and later caused undefined "
"behavior in string operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:896
msgid "(`gh-32296 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32296>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:898
msgid ""
"Some reductions that use `out=` with a less precise dtype than the inputs/"
"`dtype=` may now return different, more precise, results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:903
msgid "`np.spacing` with NaN input no longer emits a `RuntimeWarning`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:905
msgid "(`gh-32602 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32602>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:907
msgid ""
"``pinv`` with ``rtol=None`` did not select the correct output dtype for "
"integer input. It now always returns float results for integer input and no "
"longer spuriously raises ValueError for some inputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:911
msgid "(`gh-32679 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32679>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:913
msgid ""
"``np.histogramdd`` now converts and returns a plain ndarray as the other "
"histogramming functions do. Previously it only did that when it was handed a "
"sequence of arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:916
msgid "(`gh-32701 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32701>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:918
msgid ""
"Doing ``v[...,]`` on a void scalar previously returned a ``np.void`` scalar "
"while ``v[...]`` returned a 0d array.  Both now return a 0d array, matching "
"the behaviour of every other scalar type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:921
msgid "(`gh-32744 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32744>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:924
msgid "``numpy.unwrap`` behavior changes for edge cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:925
msgid ""
"An explicitly typed ``discont`` argument passed to `numpy.unwrap` wider than "
"the result dtype is now compared at the result dtype rather than promoting. "
"This may change the result of `numpy.unwrap` by ~1 ULP."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:929
msgid ""
"Calling `numpy.unwrap` with an unsigned integer ``period`` that cannot "
"represent the values needed internally now raises a `TypeError` (\"no loop "
"found\" ufunc error, reporting the mismatched dtypes) instead of the "
"``OverflowError`` raised by the previous Python implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:934
msgid "(`gh-9959 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/9959>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:937
msgid "``f2py`` line wrapping no longer produces invalid continuation lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:938
msgid ""
"Lines exceeding the column limit in ``f2py``-generated Fortran wrappers are "
"now split correctly for both fixed-form and free-form source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:941
msgid "(`gh-30967 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/30967>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:944
msgid "``f2py`` allocatable character arrays now work correctly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:945
msgid ""
"Allocatable character arrays in ``f2py``-wrapped Fortran 90 modules no "
"longer raise ``ValueError`` when accessed after allocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:948
msgid "(`gh-30971 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/30971>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:951
msgid "NumPy's internal memory allocations now use ``PyMem_RawMalloc``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:952
msgid ""
"NumPy's internal memory allocations now use ``PyMem_RawMalloc`` instead of "
"``malloc`` and can be tracked by ``tracemalloc``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:955
msgid "(`gh-31503 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/31503>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:958
msgid "Python ``str`` ufunc operands convert with the resolved dtype"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:959
msgid ""
"A Python ``str`` scalar containing trailing nulls now preserves the trailing "
"nulls in operations with StringDType. For example, ``np.array([\"x\\0\"], "
"dtype=np.dtypes.StringDType()) == \"x\\0\"`` now gives ``[True]`` rather "
"than ``[False]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:967
msgid "``ufunc.outer`` now follows NEP 50 promotion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:968
msgid ""
"Python scalars passed to ``ufunc.outer`` were converted to arrays and thus "
"treated as strongly typed, unlike for a normal ufunc call.  They are now "
"weak, so that e.g. ``np.add.outer(1., np.zeros(3, dtype=\"float32\"))`` "
"returns a ``float32`` rather than a ``float64`` array.  As a consequence, "
"huge Python integers now raise an ``OverflowError`` here as they do for "
"``ufunc.__call__``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:974
msgid "(`gh-32090 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32090>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:977
msgid "``ufunc.at`` now follows NEP 50 promotion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:978
msgid ""
"Python scalars passed as the value operand of ``ufunc.at`` were converted to "
"arrays and thus treated as strongly typed, unlike for a normal ufunc call. "
"They are now weak, so the operation is computed in the promoted dtype of the "
"target array: e.g. ``np.add.at(arr, idx, 1)`` with a ``uint64`` array now "
"uses the ``uint64`` loop rather than ``float64``, which rounded large "
"values.  As a consequence, out-of-bounds Python integers now raise an "
"``OverflowError`` here, as they do for ``ufunc.__call__``; previously they "
"wrapped silently (e.g. adding ``-1`` to a ``uint8`` array produced 255)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:987
msgid "(`gh-32094 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32094>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:990
msgid "Legacy valgrind-based C coverage tool removed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:991
msgid ""
"The legacy C code-coverage tooling under ``tools/c_coverage/`` (which relied "
"on valgrind's callgrind tool) has been removed. C coverage is now collected "
"through ``gcov``; build with ``spin build --clean --gcov`` and run the tests "
"with ``spin test --gcov`` to generate a coverage report."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:996
msgid "(`gh-32314 <https://github.com/numpy/numpy/pull/32314>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:999
msgid ""
"``MaskedArray`` resets a fill_value that cannot be represented in a new dtype"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/notes-towncrier.rst:1000
msgid ""
"A fill_value copied from a source array is now reset to the default "
"fill_value for the new dtype when it cannot be represented in that dtype.  "
"Previously the copied value could be stale: ufuncs that change dtype left "
"the result holding a fill_value typed for the old dtype, which raised a "
"``TypeError`` only when something later validated it (such as ``.view()``), "
"and a floating point fill_value that overflows an integer dtype was kept as "
"an out-of-range value together with a ``RuntimeWarning``.  Both now fall "
"back to the default, including when a masked array is passed to "
"``MaskedArray`` with a different ``dtype``.  A fill_value given explicitly "
"by the user is still validated and raises as before.  This can now raise a "
"``ComplexWarning`` if the fill_value is complex and the new dtype is real."
msgstr ""

